// S5: Large non-pow2 3D — fixed-step RK4
// Grid 500×500×10 → CS pads 1000×1000×20; mumax3 pads 1000×1000×20 (IDENTICAL)
// mumax3 uses 2N for Z=10 (>SMALL_N=5). FFT sizes match exactly.
// 1000 = 2^3 × 5^3,  20 = 2^2 × 5  — non-pow2, 7-smooth.
// At this scale: f32 gives ~6× FFT bandwidth vs f64 (1000-size > L1 cache)
// Expected: CS VkFFT f32 wins (VkFFT + f32 combined; mumax3 is also f32 but cuFFT)
// Fair: RK4 (4 eval/step), dt=5e-14, f32

SetGridSize(500, 500, 10)
SetCellSize(2e-9, 2e-9, 3e-9)
Msat  = 860e3
Aex   = 13e-12
alpha = 0.02
setsolver(4)
FixDt = 5e-14
m = uniform(1, 0.05, 0)
B_ext = vector(0, 0, 0)
steps(NSTEPS_PLACEHOLDER)
